{
  "verdict": "request_changes",
  "summary": "The plan addresses the five prior-round findings, but the amended SDK adapter and execution handoff still have specification gaps.",
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "severity": "blocking",
      "location": "Task 9: SdkConversation notification handling and tests",
      "issue": "[P1] The plan requires a matching terminal event but does not require the final message to belong to that same thread and turn or prove that it is complete. An unrelated or partial final message could be returned as success.",
      "suggestion": "Validate the final messageΓÇÖs thread ID, turn ID, type and completeness before constructing PeerReply. Test wrong-thread, wrong-turn and partial-message cases."
    },
    {
      "severity": "important",
      "location": "Task 4: finding ID derivation",
      "issue": "[P2] IDs are derived from round, index and content without an explicit review-ID input. Reusing the legacy function unchanged could give identical findings in different review series the same ID, contrary to the required namespace.",
      "suggestion": "Bind the review ID into the deterministic hash input and test identical findings in two series."
    },
    {
      "severity": "important",
      "location": "Task 9: Bridge error handling",
      "issue": "[P2] ΓÇ£Error/uncertain paths poison the conversationΓÇ¥ includes invalid input, instance or thread mismatch, conflicts and BUSY. These errors can occur before native work; poisoning on ADAPTER_RESTARTED would also prevent the required explicit fresh conversation.",
      "suggestion": "Poison only after a turn may have started or native state becomes uncertain. Keep pre-admission refusals recoverable and test a fresh conversation after ADAPTER_RESTARTED."
    },
    {
      "severity": "important",
      "location": "Task 9: cancellation handling",
      "issue": "[P2] The plan tests cancellation and safe errors but does not require cancellation to propagate after bounded interruption and close, as the amendment specifies.",
      "suggestion": "Specify cleanup within the remaining deadline followed by cancellation propagation, and assert that behavior in the engine and SDK tests."
    },
    {
      "severity": "important",
      "location": "Task 9: codex_status and retry cache",
      "issue": "[P2] The status interface specifies only the instance ID, omitting the required owned thread ID and ready/poisoned/busy state. The cache instructions also omit the explicit requirement to retain a prompt SHA-256 rather than prompt bodies.",
      "suggestion": "Define and test all status fields, including state transitions, and specify digest-only prompt retention with full logical cache accounting."
    },
    {
      "severity": "important",
      "location": "Spec pointer and Task 9 test command",
      "issue": "[P2] The plan still names commit 5c93d6b29d507ace5e7ad901e75a188924204ba2 as the exact approved spec, while the trusted amended approval identifies commit efdf3589c26941372e1c8c6a8a450f1ccc82f9e4 and spec blob f9b94a453e2c6248dd80c3f6d31be8178c7237e4. Task 9 also invokes tests/support/collaborative_command.py, which is neither defined nor listed among Task 0ΓÇÖs supervised helpers.",
      "suggestion": "Point the execution handoff at the amended approved blob and run Task 9 tests through the defined Task 0 owner, or define that wrapper with the same supervision contract."
    }
  ]
}
